{"kind":"assert","text":"Planner N1 revision 2 direction, 2026-10-04. I read all 771 lines (40,995 bytes) of notes/2026-10-03-proposal-artifact-reads.md at b4b06d2649aff2946772747cfc383305d3ba2f43. The 41b304e7-to-b4b06d26 inventory changes that note only: both frozen 006 files and their separate provenance are unchanged. Revision 2 materially applies 25b6: new whole-tree disclosure, final authorization judgment, graph ordering and boundary-parent snapshots, root/merge presentation, missing-object failure, bounded raw headers, MCP slicing ownership, retention scope, transport failure grammar and the full cold-review journey. Preserve these repairs and the original complete N1/C5/C6/MCP scope.\n\n1. Choose the actual comparison record for the next design. Section 4.1 still cannot infer the actual proposal-time comparison from equality of a path/status list. Different baseline trees can produce the same paths and statuses while showing different content; a multi-base union can equal one base's path list. An empty-tree first proposal can itself have no changed paths, so base=head plus changed=[] also does not prove which history set is intended. Remove the claim that a matching candidate is the exact original comparison, and the unconditional statement that several bases cannot be reproduced by one base's paths. Record, for future generations, the comparison the producer actually used: empty tree, or the complete deterministically ordered merge-base IDs, including the single head/base case. The exact design must state the added proposal/persistence/export/replay-context field, producer and consumers, supported old/new representation and composed contract text. This is direction to finish the N1 design and implementing-lane handoff, not authorization to change the pending release, verifier or admission now. Do not invent a new verifier gate or alter old proposal admission. For old generations without retained proof of the actual comparison, return an explicitly qualified legacy comparison. A reachable recorded base may support a clearly labelled candidate diff; do not claim it was the actual single base, one of several, or that the Room list must be larger. Do not guess from today's main. New multi-base generations should identify all actual bases; if the client cannot present an exact single diff, say that instead of silently choosing one. Keep head files and recorded changed paths available. If a candidate inference is retained as a presentation heuristic, name it as such, bound up to two tree comparisons plus reachability/object reads, and distinguish missing retained objects from an unknown comparison.\n\n2. Align permitted snapshots and history bounds. R-ART-1 currently lists only the commit set and its parents, but file(head) must work when that set is empty or its walk is too large. Explicitly permit the recorded head independently of listing history; permit actual retained comparison commits and the validated boundary parents the adapter needs. Never serve an unrelated recorded base as proposal content merely because it is readable through main. Main's current reachability is not a proposal-retention promise. A work bound on commit reads can be hit even when the resulting set is small: state that separately from set size, and do not let history-walk failure turn a readable head file into too-large. For multiple actual bases define the history exclusion set and each parent's scope coherently. Keep bounded path reads, no arbitrary blob-ID access.\n\n3. Make the encoded-response limit real. Section 7 says a 2 MiB encoded answer cannot arise and would be internal. That is false: valid UTF-8 file text can expand sixfold through JSON escaping, and 1,000 paths of up to 4,096 bytes already exceed 2 MiB before encoding. Treat the response budget as an ordinary documented size boundary, with a stable too-large/partial result where appropriate, not an internal failure. Page by both item and encoded-byte limits; a byte-ended page must progress and have the same query-bound cursor. Specify the result when one item or one file cannot fit. Distinguish the logical file-content limit from the transport budget. Also say how the adapter bounds blob acquisition itself (bounded metadata/range/stream or an explicit unsupported-provider result), rather than downloading an arbitrarily large blob before checking its size. Exact cache/read-work constants can remain proposed implementation choices; no per-field test sweep is requested.\n\n4. Correct the identity and evidence promises. Every successful or qualified artifact result needs its resolved generation/head/comparison and, for a file, the actual snapshot commit or empty tree and path; a not-in-proposal or unresolved-comparison result should also retain the requested target/path where needed. Either carry available identity on size and head-mismatch results or narrow the statement 'every answer' to the actual types; null and transport errors cannot carry that promise. Keep latest advisory and current authority uncached. Say that displayed diffs and author change IDs do not themselves constitute recorded Room evidence, settle a review or override authoritative admission/carry/outcomes. Human reviewers may of course use the immutable content and displayed diff to form a review; 'never evidence for review' should not suggest that they cannot.\n\nRevise the compact acceptance to cover the comparison ambiguity and one encoded-byte boundary economically, updating the exact amendment and A1-A7 dependencies together. Reuse legitimate witnesses where possible; do not add row-mirroring tests or perform runtime work for this planning correction. The full member/reader matrix, immutable no-transcript review, line-bound question, revision, evidence distinctions, publication watermark, all MCP obligations and separate private C1 authority remain owed. Exact independent Architecture/Security/Simplification design review and adoption precede any implementing commission. The pending all-47 a23 release review at d691, automated reviewer restriction, 10x test-cost priority and builder first-useful-Jam readiness are unchanged. No tests, build, installation, provider action, source edit or root commit was performed.","body":{"head":"b4b06d2649aff2946772747cfc383305d3ba2f43","no_git_artifact":"true","scope":"N1 revision 2 full-read direction and comparison-record design choice; no adoption or runtime commission.","source_approval":"none"}}